] [17592186341787 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341787 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341787 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186339910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341787 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e58edcff-ee66-5f0c-86cd-1ec279fff31c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452782 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452783 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452784 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "020f4792-4587-5aa1-be12-a9175f71b2e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354530 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/62/62925844de27c9731b181f17a1bdd912bfa3265176bd62ebda425d182ae8d9e8.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not completely cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$ Also, the integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385325 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6de75fa4-40ed-54ed-9a38-aaf2ba31ee58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385326 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1337dd4f-9280-53a2-a0bf-10fa5a1172ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385327 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385327 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385327 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d3b06213-6b70-5fb1-9074-bd29c49e8d32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385328 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385328 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385328 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385329 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385329 #edb/ref 1082